{"id":"hysteresis","path":"docs/modules/hysteresis/eli5.md","title":"Module 1: Hysteresis - The Memory Cell's P-E Curve","category":"Learning","sha256":"c4ca870e27ef915aeb651cd443c7967b1f40e31725a28ba322b01b95a2210fa9","rights":"MIT","attribution":"FeCIM Lattice Tools contributors (repository-authored Markdown; publisher assets excluded)","bytes":5464,"terms":["Ec","FeCIM","HZO","Hysteresis Loop","Pr","Preisach Model","Remnant Polarization"],"headings":[{"text":"Module 1: Hysteresis - The Memory Cell's P-E Curve","level":1,"anchor":"module-1-hysteresis---the-memory-cells-p-e-curve"},{"text":"Evidence Status (Demonstrated vs Modeled vs Aspirational)","level":2,"anchor":"evidence-status-demonstrated-vs-modeled-vs-aspirational"},{"text":"The Core Problem: How Does a Memory Cell Remember?","level":2,"anchor":"the-core-problem-how-does-a-memory-cell-remember"},{"text":"What is Polarization?","level":2,"anchor":"what-is-polarization"},{"text":"The Hysteresis Loop (The Main Idea)","level":2,"anchor":"the-hysteresis-loop-the-main-idea"},{"text":"Why This Matters for Memory","level":2,"anchor":"why-this-matters-for-memory"},{"text":"The Three Key Numbers for HZO","level":2,"anchor":"the-three-key-numbers-for-hzo"},{"text":"The Preisach Model (How We Simulate It)","level":2,"anchor":"the-preisach-model-how-we-simulate-it"},{"text":"Our Simplified Version: Tanh Function","level":2,"anchor":"our-simplified-version-tanh-function"},{"text":"What the Demo Shows You","level":2,"anchor":"what-the-demo-shows-you"},{"text":"How to Run Module 1","level":2,"anchor":"how-to-run-module-1"},{"text":"Key Takeaways","level":2,"anchor":"key-takeaways"},{"text":"Next Steps","level":2,"anchor":"next-steps"}],"nodes":[{"kind":"heading","level":1,"anchor":"module-1-hysteresis---the-memory-cells-p-e-curve","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 1: Hysteresis - The Memory Cell's P-E Curve"}]},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"evidence-status-demonstrated-vs-modeled-vs-aspirational","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Evidence Status (Demonstrated vs Modeled vs Aspirational)"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Demonstrated:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" P-E hysteresis curves, Preisach model, LK solver, material presets are implemented in this repo and verifiable from source/tests."}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Modeled:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" ISPP write controller, retention/wakeup/dispersion are simulator models unless explicitly tied to cited measured data."}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Aspirational:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Real device calibration and fabrication validation are roadmap intent and must not be reported as demonstrated results."}]}]}]},{"kind":"quote","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explain Like I'm 5:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" The ferroelectric material remembers which way you pushed it"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-core-problem-how-does-a-memory-cell-remember","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Core Problem: How Does a Memory Cell Remember?"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Regular materials behave like a spring:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Push the spring → it compresses\nStop pushing → it springs back to normal\nNo memory!\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ferroelectric materials (like HZO) behave like a stubborn kid:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Push left → stays pushed left!\nPush right → stays pushed right!\n(doesn't naturally bounce back)\n\nThat's how it remembers! 🧠\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"what-is-polarization","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is Polarization?"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Inside materials, positive (+) and negative (-) charges can separate:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Before:                After pushing:\n  ⊕⊖                     ⊕────⊖\n(together)            (separated = polarized)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polarization (P)"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" = how much the charges are separated."}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-hysteresis-loop-the-main-idea","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Hysteresis Loop (The Main Idea)"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When you push and release, the polarization traces a loop:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"        Polarization (P)\n              ↑\n         Ps ──┼────────╮      Ps = saturation\n              │        │           (maximum)\n         Pr ──┼─╮      │      Pr = remanent\n              │ │      │           (stays when V=0)\n    ──────────┼─●──────●────→ Voltage (V)\n              │       │ │\n        -Pr ──┼───────╯ │\n              │         │\n        -Ps ──┼─────────╯\n              │\n            -Ec  0  +Ec\n\n        Ec = coercive field\n            (voltage needed to flip)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The key insight:"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Going UP is NOT the same as going DOWN"},{"kind":"text","text":"! The material remembers where it came from."}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"why-this-matters-for-memory","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Why This Matters for Memory"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"Normal memory: ON or OFF (1 bit)\n              ░░░░░░░░░░\n              bit = 0 or 1\n\nFerroelectric: Stop at different points on the loop!\n              ░░░░░░░░░░\n              State 0 ●\n              State 1 ●\n              State 2 ●\n              ... (30-level simulator baseline)\n\nMore modeled levels per cell can represent more information in the simulation; real devices need separate validation.\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-three-key-numbers-for-hzo","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Three Key Numbers for HZO"}]},{"kind":"table","children":[{"kind":"table-head","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Parameter"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Symbol"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Value"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Why It Matters"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Saturation Polarization"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ps"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"30 μC/cm²"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Maximum charge separation (memory capacity)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Coercive Field"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ec"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1.2 MV/cm"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Voltage to flip the polarization (write effort)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Remanent"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pr"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"~"},{"kind":"text","text":"24.5 μC/cm²"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What stays after you stop pushing (what you read)"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"the-preisach-model-how-we-simulate-it","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The Preisach Model (How We Simulate It)"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Real materials have trillions of atoms. We can't simulate each one"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Instead, imagine the material is made of millions of tiny switches called "},{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hysterons"}]},{"kind":"text","text":":"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"One Hysteron (a tiny sticky switch):\n\nOutput (+1 or -1)\n    (+1) ├───────────────────╮\n         │         α         │\n     (0) ├───────────────────┼──→ Input Voltage\n         │         β         │\n    (-1) ├───────────────────╯\n\nα = voltage to turn ON\nβ = voltage to turn OFF\n(they're different!)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each hysteron:"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Turns ON at voltage α (and stays ON)"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Turns OFF at voltage β (and stays OFF)"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ignores the input between β and α"}]}]}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The whole hysteresis loop comes from adding up millions of hysterons"},{"kind":"text","text":"!"}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"our-simplified-version-tanh-function","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Our Simplified Version: Tanh Function"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Instead of millions of hysterons, we use a smooth formula:"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"P = Ps × tanh((V - Ec) / δ)\n"},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This gives us:"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A smooth S-shaped curve"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Similar shape to real data"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fast to compute"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Easy to understand"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"what-the-demo-shows-you","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What the Demo Shows You"}]},{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When you run Module 1, you see:"}]},{"kind":"list","ordered":true,"children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interactive P-E Curve"}]},{"kind":"text","text":": Drag voltage up/down, watch polarization follow"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Material Selector"}]},{"kind":"text","text":": Default HZO, Optimized, Ferroelectric CIM"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Waveform Modes"}]},{"kind":"text","text":":"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sine: Smooth oscillation"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Triangle: Linear up/down"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Square: Snap to extremes"}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Manual: You control it"}]}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"30-Level Baseline"}]},{"kind":"text","text":": Visualization of configurable multi-level storage assumptions"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"how-to-run-module-1","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to Run Module 1"}]},{"kind":"pre","text":"go build -o fecim-lattice-tools ./cmd/fecim-lattice-tools\n./fecim-lattice-tools hysteresis\n"},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"key-takeaways","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Key Takeaways"}]},{"kind":"table","children":[{"kind":"table-head","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Concept"}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Remember This"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polarization"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How separated the charges are (storage amount)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hysteresis"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The loop shape shows memory (up ≠ down)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Coercive Field"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Voltage needed to flip (write effort)"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"30 Levels"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Simulator baseline for configurable discrete storage assumptions"}]}]},{"kind":"row","children":[{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Preisach Model"}]}]},{"kind":"cell","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Simulates hysteresis using tiny hysterons"}]}]}]},{"kind":"rule"},{"kind":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"next-steps","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next Steps"}]},{"kind":"list","children":[{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Want to see it compute?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Go to "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:crossbar","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 2: Crossbar"}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Want to recognize digits?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" Go to "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:mnist","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Module 3: MNIST"}]}]}]},{"kind":"item","children":[{"kind":"paragraph","children":[{"kind":"strong","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Back to overview?"}]},{"kind":"text","text":" See "},{"kind":"link","url":"doc:curriculum","children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ELI5 Overview"}]}]}]}]}]}
